    "description": "<p>Assume the complete Crouzeix bound and the analytic Faber coefficient estimate stated in the paper. Let A be a complex matrix of order at most four, and let P be a matrix-valued polynomial of arbitrary finite degree and coefficient size. If ||P[A]|| = 2 max_{W(A)} ||P|| &gt; 0, we prove that there are constant unit coefficient vectors u, v for which p = v* P u attains the same equality. Jin's scalar rigidity theorem then implies that W(A) is a disk, and the extracted scalar polynomial is a monomial after centering and scaling that disk. The main step converts zero slack in a positive boundary-field inequality into a rank-one condition on the coefficient factors of extremal singular vectors. An elementary Hermitian-pencil argument supplies the required regular boundary arc in dimension four.</p>",
    "references": [
      {
        "reference": "P. Åhag, R. Czyż, and J. Virtanen, The Complete Crouzeix Conjecture in Dimension Three and the Clouâtre-Ostermann-Ransford conjecture, arXiv:2608.27346v4 (2026). https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.27346v4."
      },
      {
        "reference": "S. Jin, Rigidity at the Extremal Crouzeix Constant, Preprints.org, version 2, 15 September 2026. https://www.preprints.org/manuscript/202609.0079/v2."
      },
      {
        "reference": "OpenAI, A direct proof of the complete Crouzeix inequality, 26 September 2026. Repository revision fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb. https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/A-direct-proof-of-the-complete-Crouzeix-inequality-September-26-2026/build/main.tex."
      },
      {
        "reference": "OpenAI, The complete Crouzeix theorem: optimal similarity and a common positive boundary representation, 23 September 2026. Repository revision fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb. https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/The-complete-Crouzeix-theorem-September-23-2026/build/main.tex."
      }
